# Chess Arena Project Rules

## Code Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode
- Prefer functional programming over OOP
- Keep functions short (<20 lines)
- Use descriptive names for variables and functions
- Avoid magic numbers and strings
- Use JSDoc for complex functions

## Architecture
- Strict separation of layers: core (pure logic), state, UI
- Immutable data where possible
- Pure functions for game logic
- Use interfaces for data structures
- Keep dependencies minimal

## Testing
- Write unit tests for all core logic
- Test edge cases
- Use Vitest for testing
- Run tests before committing

## Git
- Use conventional commits
- Keep commits small and focused
- Write clear commit messages

## Documentation
- Document complex logic
- Keep README.md up to date
- Document architecture decisions in ARCHITECTURE.md

## Performance
- Optimize critical paths
- Avoid unnecessary re-renders
- Use Web Workers for heavy computations

## Accessibility
- Follow WCAG guidelines
- Use semantic HTML
- Provide ARIA labels
- Ensure keyboard navigation

## Internationalization
- Use i18n for all user-facing text
- Keep translations up to date

## Security
- Validate all inputs
- Sanitize outputs
- Avoid eval()

## Deployment
- Ensure all tests pass before deployment
- Optimize bundle size
- Use GitHub Pages or Netlify for deployment
